  "finding": "The proposal derives c_l = clip((1/Q_l - 1)/(rho_l^2 + 1e-8), 1e-4, 0.99/max|z|^2). The cap exists to keep exp_0^c inside the ball, but with rho_l ~ mean|z| and max|z| a small multiple of it, the cap binds for every Q below about 0.95: c_l becomes the constant 0.99/max|z|^2 and no longer depends on the measured behaviour. A trained arm would be a fixed-curvature arm carrying a behaviour-shaped label, which the scope contract's joint-coupling test rejects.",
